{"audio": "1corinthians-13.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 93333, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2800, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Thirteen."}, {"start_ms": 2800, "end_ms": 11467, "text": "Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal."}, {"start_ms": 11467, "end_ms": 22000, "text": "And though I have the gift of prophecy, and understand all mysteries, and all knowledge; and though I have all faith, so that I could remove mountains, and have not charity, I am nothing."}, {"start_ms": 22000, "end_ms": 30000, "text": "And though I bestow all my goods to feed the poor, and though I give my body to be burned, and have not charity, it profiteth me nothing."}, {"start_ms": 30000, "end_ms": 50000, "text": "Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up, Doth not behave itself unseemly, seeketh not her own, is not easily provoked, thinketh no evil; Rejoiceth not in iniquity, but rejoiceth in the truth; Beareth all things, believeth all things,"}, {"start_ms": 50000, "end_ms": 52800, "text": "hopeth all things, endureth all things."}, {"start_ms": 52800, "end_ms": 62000, "text": "Charity never faileth: but whether there be prophecies, they shall fail; whether there be tongues, they shall cease; whether there be knowledge, it shall vanish away."}, {"start_ms": 62000, "end_ms": 65067, "text": "For we know in part, and we prophesy in part."}, {"start_ms": 65067, "end_ms": 70000, "text": "But when that which is perfect is come, then that which is in part shall be done away."}, {"start_ms": 70000, "end_ms": 78933, "text": "When I was a child, I spake as a child, I understood as a child, I thought as a child: but when I became a man, I put away childish things."}, {"start_ms": 78933, "end_ms": 87733, "text": "For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as als